From 937e1c7417240c8bb82617954c23c24ec1d45eb0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephanie Sithu <sesith01@louisville.edu>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 22:32:28 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] top: add PWR column fed by syspower's measuring code

Each refresh, syspower's code (src/top/syspower) measures whole-system
power. Each task gets the share of those watts matching its share of
all CPU time on the machine.

- copy syspower's grp/hw/mdl/ut code, add grp_step() and a small API
  (sp_init, sp_sample) so top.c never sees syspower's macros
- build it as libsyspower.la and link it into top (needs hwloc, udev)
- PWR column right after %CPU, up to 3 decimals; '-' when not root
- start as a flat list instead of tree view, like Ubuntu's top
- errors go to /var/tmp/top-syspower.log; TOP_SYSPOWER_DEBUG=1 also
  logs every measurement

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
