+# syspower inside top
+
+Power-measuring code from [syspower](https://github.com/UOFL-CSL/syspower), compiled into `top` to fill the **PWR** column.
+
+**Source:** syspower commit `c129213` plus the blank-name fix in `src/hw/hw.c`. That fix stops `hw_match()` from matching every part when a device has no model name.
+
+## What's here
+
+| Path | What it is |
+|---|---|
+| `src/` | Copied from syspower's `src/`, keeping its folder layout so its `#include <src/...>` lines still work. Left out: `main.c`, the makefiles, and `mdl/nvml/nvml.c`. |
+| `sp_top.h` | The only file `top.c` includes. It declares `sp_init()` and `sp_sample()`. |
+| `sp_top.c` | Connects top to syspower: sets up the hardware groups, measures them, and logs errors. |
+| `sp_config.h` | Force-included before every syspower file (see `Makefile.am`). It defines `NAME` and sends syspower's error messages to `/var/tmp/top-syspower.log`. |
+| `nvml_stub.c` | Stand-in for the NVIDIA GPU model, which needs CUDA's `nvml.h`. |
+
+## Changes made to the copied syspower files
+
+- `src/grp/grp.c`, `src/grp/grp.h`: added `grp_step()`, which measures every group once without printing.
+- `src/dconf.h`: wrapped `CFG_PRINTF_ERR` in `#ifndef` so `sp_config.h` can redirect it.
diff --git a/src/top/syspower/nvml_stub.c b/src/top/syspower/nvml_stub.c
new file mode 100644
index 00000000..00e12c9a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/top/syspower/nvml_stub.c
@@ -0,0 +1,15 @@
+/*
+ * Stand-in for syspower's NVIDIA GPU model (src/mdl/nvml/nvml.c).
+ * The real one needs NVIDIA's nvml.h, which normally only comes with CUDA.
+ * Returning an error means "this model can't measure", so GPU groups
+ * (only created for known NVIDIA parts) report a failed measurement.
+ */
+#include <src/dconf.h> // syspower's headers need this first
+#include <src/grp/grp.h>
+#include <src/mdl/nvml/nvml.h>
+
+int mdl_nvml_gpu(struct grp_group *grp)
+{
+	(void)grp;
+	return -1;
+}
